## Final Judgement
##Summary of Key Insights
The fact-check found that the National Testing Agency (NTA) initially declared Mridul Rawat as failed in the NEET 2020 results, but after rechecking he emerged as the all-India topper in the Scheduled Tribe (ST) category. However, the overall all-India topper was Soyeb Aftab (720/720). Reputable news outlets (Livemint, Business Today) reported this as a blunder, while another source (NDTV) states that the NTA denied any errors, calling such claims "fake, fabricated." Thus, there is direct conflict between evidence supporting the occurrence of a blunder and evidence that the NTA refuted any error.

## Conclusion
The claim that the NTA made a major blunder by stating that the all-India topper had failed is supported by some sources (which confirm an error regarding a category topper) but contradicted by the NTA’s own denial of any errors. Additionally, the phrasing “all India topper” is ambiguous—it could refer to the overall topper (which was not involved) or a category topper. Given the presence of both supporting and refuting evidence from multiple sources, the most appropriate decision is `conflicting evidence`.

### Verdict: CONFLICTING

### Justification
The National Testing Agency (NTA) initially declared Mridul Rawat as failed in the NEET 2020 results, but after rechecking he emerged as the all-India topper in the Scheduled Tribe (ST) category ([Livemint](https://www.livemint.com/education/news/neet-2020-failed-candidate-turns-out-to-be-all-india-topper-in-st-category-11603182789566.html)). This was reported as a "major blunder" by news outlets ([Business Today](https://www.businesstoday.in/latest/trends/story/major-blunder-in-neet-results-student-who-failed-found-to-be-the-topper-276333-2020-10-20)). However, the overall all-India topper was Soyeb Aftab (720/720), and the NTA itself denied any errors, calling such claims "fake, fabricated" ([NDTV](https://www.ndtv.com/education/claims-of-errors-in-neet-2020-results-fake-fabricated-nta-2313136)). Therefore, the evidence is conflicting.